<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/"><channel><title>News from Google</title><link>https://blog.google/</link><description>News from Google</description><atom:link href="https://blog.google/rss/" rel="self"/><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><image><url>https://blog.google/static/blogv2/images/google.png</url><title>News from Google</title><link>https://blog.google/</link></image><item><title>Wheels up: Trends and tips for 2026 holiday travel</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/holiday-travel-trends-2026/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Holiday_Trends_gradient_hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Illustration of family traveling</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Holiday_Trends_gradient_hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Explore this year’s trends and tips for holiday travel — from insights on booking the lowest fare to trending destinations for Thanksgiving and Christmas.</description><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/holiday-travel-trends-2026/</guid><category>Search</category><category>Travel</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Wheels up: Trends and tips for 2026 holiday travel</title><description>Explore this year’s trends and tips for holiday travel — from insights on booking the lowest fare to trending destinations for Thanksgiving and Christmas.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/holiday-travel-trends-2026/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>James Byers</name><title>Group Product Manager, Search</title><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>Making AI training available to UK and Ireland educators</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/education/making-ai-training-available-to-uk-and-ireland-educators/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/ISTE_2026_Collections_BlogHeade.max-600x600.format-webp_CkzTCJX.webp" width="540"/><media:description>A collage of floating Google Workspace for Education interface elements on a soft, light background.</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/ISTE_2026_Collections_BlogHeade.max-600x600.format-webp_CkzTCJX.webp"&gt;Google's AI tools aim to help educators achieve their teaching goals and provide students with personalized learning experiences.</description><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 07:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/education/making-ai-training-available-to-uk-and-ireland-educators/</guid><category>Learning &amp; Education</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Making AI training available to UK and Ireland educators</title><description>Google's AI tools aim to help educators achieve their teaching goals and provide students with personalized learning experiences.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/education/making-ai-training-available-to-uk-and-ireland-educators/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Fiona Law</name><title>Head of New Partnerships</title><department>Education</department><company/></author><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Grace Kelly</name><title>Digital Transformation Lead</title><department>Education</department><company/></author></item><item><title>The latest AI news we announced in September 2026</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/ai/google-ai-updates-september-2026/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/September_AI_Recap_hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>A video showing the September AI updates</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/September_AI_Recap_hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Here are Google’s latest AI updates from September 2026</description><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/ai/google-ai-updates-september-2026/</guid><category>Google DeepMind</category><category>Googlebook</category><category>AI</category><category>Gemini App</category><category>Gemini models</category><category>Google Research</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>The latest AI news we announced in September 2026</title><description>Here are Google’s latest AI updates from September 2026</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/ai/google-ai-updates-september-2026/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Blog Team</name><title/><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>Our Project Suncatcher prototype satellite is in orbit.</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-research/project-suncatcher-prototype/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/original_videos/wagtailvideo-fgyv69rc_thumb.jpg" width="540"/><media:description>Video showing a rocket launch</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/original_videos/wagtailvideo-fgyv69rc_thumb.jpg"&gt;Google's prototype satellite for Project Suncatcher, built in partnership with Planet, launched into orbit aboard the Transporter-18 rideshare mission with SpaceX.</description><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 23:30:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-research/project-suncatcher-prototype/</guid><category>Google Research</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Our Project Suncatcher prototype satellite is in orbit.</title><description/><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-research/project-suncatcher-prototype/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Travis Beals</name><title>Senior Director</title><department>Paradigms of Intelligence</department><company/></author></item><item><title>Turn your existing social assets into high-impact YouTube ads.</title><link>https://blog.google/products/ads-commerce/creating-assets-youtube-ads/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/S2E5_thumbnail.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/S2E5_thumbnail.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;In this Ads Decoded episode, we discuss ad creative — and how it can make or break your YouTube campaigns.</description><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products/ads-commerce/creating-assets-youtube-ads/</guid><category>Google Ads</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Turn your existing social assets into high-impact YouTube ads.</title><description/><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products/ads-commerce/creating-assets-youtube-ads/</url></og></item><item><title>Guided Vision in Gemini Live: built for accessibility</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/products/gemini-app/guided-vision-gemini-live/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/GuidedVision_hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>stylized hero image reading "Guided Vision"</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/GuidedVision_hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Guided Vision in Gemini Live is built alongside the blind and low-vision community and offers real-time visual assistance.</description><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/products/gemini-app/guided-vision-gemini-live/</guid><category>Gemini App</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Guided Vision in Gemini Live: built for accessibility</title><description>Guided Vision in Gemini Live is built alongside the blind and low-vision community and offers real-time visual assistance.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/products/gemini-app/guided-vision-gemini-live/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Isha Sheth</name><title>Senior Product Manager</title><department>Gemini Live</department><company/></author><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Scott Adams</name><title>Senior Product Manager</title><department>Google Accessibility Engineering</department><company/></author></item><item><title>1,400 educators joined our Badge-a-thon: Day of AI Learning.</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/education/ai-educator-series-badge-a-thon/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/original_videos/wagtailvideo-mx6wrk7a_thumb.jpg" width="540"/><media:description>Many stars bursting out of a laptop</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/original_videos/wagtailvideo-mx6wrk7a_thumb.jpg"&gt;1,400 educators earned 4,000+ digital badges at the Google Badge-a-thon. Watch the on-demand sessions on YouTube and claim your first badge today.</description><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/education/ai-educator-series-badge-a-thon/</guid><category>Learning &amp; Education</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>1,400 educators joined our Badge-a-thon: Day of AI Learning.</title><description/><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/education/ai-educator-series-badge-a-thon/</url></og></item><item><title>5 ways Search can help you perfect your at-home coffee routine</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/coffee-tips-google-search/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/SearchCoffee_hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Google AI-created image showing a latte in a cup, with latte art of a magnifying glass and Gemini spark</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/SearchCoffee_hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Learn how Google Search can help you improve your morning cup of coffee.</description><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/coffee-tips-google-search/</guid><category>Search</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>5 ways Search can help you perfect your at-home coffee routine</title><description>Learn how Google Search can help you improve your morning cup of coffee.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/coffee-tips-google-search/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Megan Stoner</name><title>Contributor</title><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>Google's AI ranks #1 for predicting flu hospitalizations.</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-research/google-science-ai-flu-forecasts/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Flusight_socialhero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Flusight_socialhero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Google’s science AI model was the best at forecasting flu-related hospital admissions, the Centers for Disease Control announced.</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:30:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-research/google-science-ai-flu-forecasts/</guid><category>Google Research</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Google's AI ranks #1 for predicting flu hospitalizations.</title><description/><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-research/google-science-ai-flu-forecasts/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Zahra Shamsi</name><title>Google Research</title><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>Gemini 4 Argon: our next era of frontier intelligence</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/gemini-4-argon/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/g4_30-09-26_key-art_blog.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Stylized promotional blog key art graphic with modern editorial branding and the text "Gemini 4 Argon"</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/g4_30-09-26_key-art_blog.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Announcing Gemini 4 Argon, our frontier model for real-world coding, enterprise knowledge work, and cyber defense, rolling out soon.</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/gemini-4-argon/</guid><category>Gemini models</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Gemini 4 Argon: our next era of frontier intelligence</title><description>Announcing Gemini 4 Argon, our frontier model for real-world coding, enterprise knowledge work, and cyber defense, rolling out soon.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/gemini-4-argon/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Koray Kavukcuoglu</name><title>SVP, Google DeepMind and Chief AI Architect, Google</title><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>Google is supporting water resilience in Chile.</title><link>https://blog.google/company-news/outreach-and-initiatives/sustainability/water-resilience-chile/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/WaterChile_socialshare.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/WaterChile_socialshare.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Google is investing $1.2M to line Chile's Unidos de Buin canal, saving 1.9 billion gallons of water annually. See how we boost watershed health.</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 18:34:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/company-news/outreach-and-initiatives/sustainability/water-resilience-chile/</guid><category>Google Cloud</category><category>Google in Latin America</category><category>Sustainability</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Google is supporting water resilience in Chile.</title><description/><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/company-news/outreach-and-initiatives/sustainability/water-resilience-chile/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Ben Townsend</name><title>Head of Infrastructure &amp; Sustainability</title><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>More partners are joining the Alliance for America’s Skilled Trades.</title><link>https://blog.google/company-news/outreach-and-initiatives/creating-opportunity/alliance-americas-skilled-trades-expands/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Skilled_Trades_social.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Skilled_Trades_social.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;The Alliance for America’s Skilled Trades is expanding, welcoming 14 new partners to accelerate training and career access nationwide.For every 100 skilled trades worker…</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 18:15:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/company-news/outreach-and-initiatives/creating-opportunity/alliance-americas-skilled-trades-expands/</guid><category>Creating opportunity</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>More partners are joining the Alliance for America’s Skilled Trades.</title><description/><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/company-news/outreach-and-initiatives/creating-opportunity/alliance-americas-skilled-trades-expands/</url></og></item><item><title>Supporting AI readiness in higher education</title><link>https://blog.google/company-news/outreach-and-initiatives/google-org/educause-2026/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/ORG-44_Blog_Header_EDUCAUSE.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Graduation caps and icons in different colors</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/ORG-44_Blog_Header_EDUCAUSE.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;At the EDUCAUSE annual conference, Google.org announced its support of three higher education initiatives to scale ethical AI readiness, modernize institutional planning…</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:43:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/company-news/outreach-and-initiatives/google-org/educause-2026/</guid><category>Learning &amp; Education</category><category>Google.org</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Supporting AI readiness in higher education</title><description/><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/company-news/outreach-and-initiatives/google-org/educause-2026/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>News from Google Team</name><title/><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>Let skills in Gemini tackle your most repetitive tasks</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/gemini/automate-tasks-with-skills/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Skills_thumbnail.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Example skill for presentation prep</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Skills_thumbnail.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Now you can automate your most repetitive tasks more easily with reusable custom instructions through skills, which will be replacing gems.</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/gemini/automate-tasks-with-skills/</guid><category>Gemini</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Let skills in Gemini tackle your most repetitive tasks</title><description>Now you can automate your most repetitive tasks more easily with reusable custom instructions through skills, which will be replacing gems.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/gemini/automate-tasks-with-skills/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Deven Tokuno</name><title>Senior Product Manager</title><department>Gemini App</department><company/></author></item><item><title>Celebrating International Translation Day: Meet 3 linguistic experts behind Google Translate</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/translate/international-translation-day-2026/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/International_Translate_Day_Blo.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>The illustration shows people around the world using Google Translate.</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/International_Translate_Day_Blo.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;On International Translation Day, learn how members of our team bring cultural nuance to Translate to connect people globally.</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/translate/international-translation-day-2026/</guid><category>Search</category><category>Translate</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Celebrating International Translation Day: Meet 3 linguistic experts behind Google Translate</title><description>On International Translation Day, learn how members of our team bring cultural nuance to Translate to connect people globally.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/translate/international-translation-day-2026/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>News from Google Team</name><title/><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>Waze rolls out new features to support Breast Cancer Awareness Month.</title><link>https://blog.google/waze/breast-cancer-awareness-month/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/BreastCancerCampaign_KeyVisual.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/BreastCancerCampaign_KeyVisual.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;This October, Waze will help drivers find screening clinics, assess their health risks, and schedule routine checkups.</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/waze/breast-cancer-awareness-month/</guid><category>Waze</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Waze rolls out new features to support Breast Cancer Awareness Month.</title><description/><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/waze/breast-cancer-awareness-month/</url></og></item><item><title>We’re introducing SynthID Bio, bringing our watermarking technology to synthetic biology.</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-deepmind/synthid-bio/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/BioSynthID_socialshare.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/BioSynthID_socialshare.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Google DeepMind introduces SynthID Bio to watermark AI-designed proteins while maintaining biological function. Read the full research report here.</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 15:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-deepmind/synthid-bio/</guid><category>Google DeepMind</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>We’re introducing SynthID Bio, bringing our watermarking technology to synthetic biology.</title><description/><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-deepmind/synthid-bio/</url></og></item><item><title>Game on: Henry Cavill is putting Googlebook to the test</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/devices/googlebook/henry-cavill-googlebook-video-game/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Cavill.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>: Actor Henry Cavill, with a mustache, wearing a brown ribbed knit sweater and jeans, sits at a large rustic wooden table resting his hand on an open Googlebook.</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Cavill.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Henry Cavill is partnering with Googlebook to build a video game, coming this November.</description><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/devices/googlebook/henry-cavill-googlebook-video-game/</guid><category>Googlebook</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Game on: Henry Cavill is putting Googlebook to the test</title><description>Henry Cavill is partnering with Googlebook to build a video game, coming this November.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/devices/googlebook/henry-cavill-googlebook-video-game/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Menaka Shroff</name><title>Vice President Marketing, Google – Global Android Ecosystem</title><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>Experience two artists’ perspectives on philosophy, science, and AI</title><link>https://blog.google/company-news/outreach-and-initiatives/arts-culture/las-art-foundation-ai-residency/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/LAS_x_Google_Arts__Culture_Titl.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>A behind the scenes video introducing the residency collaboration</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/LAS_x_Google_Arts__Culture_Titl.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Artists Xin Liu and Eunjo Lee used Google AI to create new artworks with LAS Art Foundation and Google Arts &amp; Culture Lab.</description><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/company-news/outreach-and-initiatives/arts-culture/las-art-foundation-ai-residency/</guid><category>Arts &amp; Culture</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Experience two artists’ perspectives on philosophy, science, and AI</title><description>Artists Xin Liu and Eunjo Lee used Google AI to create new artworks with LAS Art Foundation and Google Arts &amp; Culture Lab.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/company-news/outreach-and-initiatives/arts-culture/las-art-foundation-ai-residency/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Freya Salway</name><title>Head of the Lab, Google Arts &amp; Culture</title><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>Google is a technology partner for the launch of America.gov.</title><link>https://blog.google/company-news/outreach-and-initiatives/public-policy/america-gov-google-public-sector/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/G_gray_hero.max-600x600.format-webp_n4n8cbz.webp" width="540"/><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/G_gray_hero.max-600x600.format-webp_n4n8cbz.webp"&gt;Google partners with America.gov to use Gemini to help 100 million people access federal services faster. See how we are modernizing public access.</description><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:15:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/company-news/outreach-and-initiatives/public-policy/america-gov-google-public-sector/</guid><category>Public Policy</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Google is a technology partner for the launch of America.gov.</title><description/><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/company-news/outreach-and-initiatives/public-policy/america-gov-google-public-sector/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Jim Kelly</name><title>Vice President of Federal</title><department>Google Public Sector</department><company/></author></item></channel></rss>